    "result_text": "Green. Here's how I addressed each finding:\n\n**Finding 1 \u2014 \"dead `householdExists`\": incorrect, left as-is (with a fix).** The variable is still consumed a few lines down in the possible-duplicate suppression: `Integer possibleDuplicateOf = householdExists ? null : this.clinicService.findPossibleDuplicateOwnerId(owner)`. So it isn't leftover. What *was* stale was the comment above it referencing \"the household-duplicate rule below\" \u2014 that rule is gone, so I rewrote the comment to name the concerns the household id actually still feeds (identity key, level cap, possible-duplicate suppression).\n\nOn the related aside \u2014 dropping the household-duplicate `CONFLICT` block was not incidental. The one acceptance test creates a second owner in the same household *without* `sharesHousehold` and asserts a `2xx`; the old block returned `409` on exactly that path. So the rejection had to go for the spec's \"a new owner \u2026 among their household members\" to be reachable. Hard duplicates are still rejected via the identity-key check. I flagged this interpretation in my previous summary.\n\n**Findings 2 & 3 \u2014 valid, fixed together.** I moved the per-owner membership derivation into the domain model as `Owner.membershipPoints(Integer householdSize)` and `Owner.membershipLevel(Integer householdSize)`, which take the live household size as an explicit argument and apply the cap. Consequences:\n\n- **No entity mutation.** The service's cap computation now calls `member.membershipLevel(members.size())` \u2014 the size is passed in, so nothing primes `householdSize` on managed entities inside a read-only transaction.\n- **Computation lives in the service.** `computeMembershipLevelCap(householdId)` is now a `@Transactional(readOnly = true)` method on `ClinicService`/`ClinicServiceImpl`, alongside `findOwnersByHouseholdId`. The controller just calls `clinicService.computeMembershipLevelCap(...)`, and no longer reaches into the mapper.\n- **No duplicated band logic.** The points\u2192level thresholds exist once, in `Owner`. The mapper's `formatMembershipPoints`/`formatMembershipLevel` now delegate to the domain methods (passing the read-time `householdSize`), keeping the MapStruct `qualifiedByName` hooks intact. Removed the now-unused `LocalDate` import from the mapper.\n\nBehaviour is unchanged: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
